WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Last time, a global number came from a local reading: a kidney cell judged the

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.900
oxygen in its own patch.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.900
A cut seals in minutes, while the same clotting proteins flow through every healthy

4
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.460
vessel untouched. Where is the line drawn?

5
00:00:19.983 --> 00:00:22.103
The plug has already done one job.

6
00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:27.463
It anchored a membrane at the breach: activated platelets turn their

7
00:00:27.463 --> 00:00:31.603
phosphatidylserine outward, and so become a procoagulant surface.

8
00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:38.167
Tissue factor sits on cells beneath the lining, out of contact with blood until the

9
00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:44.987
wall breaks. Exposed, it binds factor VIIa, and that pair cuts factor X and factor

10
00:00:44.987 --> 00:00:49.467
IX. Factor Xa with Va makes a little thrombin.

11
00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:55.977
Nowhere near enough to clot anything, and it does not last: tissue factor pathway

12
00:00:55.977 --> 00:00:57.877
inhibitor shuts that assembly down.

13
00:00:59.117 --> 00:01:01.237
The trickle was never meant to clot blood.

14
00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:07.197
It is a signal: it activates platelets and cuts factors V, VIII and XI.

15
00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.310
Thrombin has built the machine that makes thrombin in bulk, and it assembles on the

16
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.310
platelet membrane.

17
00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.570
Factor IXa with VIIIa makes factor Xa, and Xa with Va cuts prothrombin.

18
00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.610
On the usual estimate, well over 90 percent of a wound's thrombin is made there.

19
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.120
Here is the one idea.

20
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.160
Thrombin is made on surfaces, not in solution.

21
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.140
A clot grows where a surface holds the enzymes, and nowhere else.

22
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:41.223
The burst does the visible work.

23
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:45.783
Thrombin cuts fibrinogen to fibrin, a mesh through the plug.

24
00:01:47.043 --> 00:01:51.683
It activates factor XIII, which cross-links the mesh against arterial pressure.

25
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:55.397
Thrombin made at the breach could drift downstream.

26
00:01:56.957 --> 00:02:02.437
Antithrombin destroys it, and on intact lining a surface sugar speeds antithrombin

27
00:02:02.437 --> 00:02:04.357
up by a hundred to a thousandfold.

28
00:02:05.777 --> 00:02:09.297
How far does thrombin get: a whole vessel, or a cell or two?

29
00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.090
One to five micrometres.

30
00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:23.870
One to a few cell thicknesses, from diffusion and decay rates: an order-of-magnitude

31
00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.370
estimate, not a measurement.

32
00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:31.530
In open plasma the reach is tens of micrometres, and flow only shortens it.

33
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:35.033
More brakes belong to the intact lining.

34
00:02:36.453 --> 00:02:41.453
Thrombomodulin turns thrombin into an activator of protein C, which inactivates

35
00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:43.413
factors Va and VIIIa.

36
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:50.113
Prostacyclin and nitric oxide keep passing platelets quiet, and later plasmin

37
00:02:50.113 --> 00:02:51.213
dissolves the fibrin.

38
00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:58.273
Read it back. The plug puts a surface where the wall breaks, the trickle switches it

39
00:02:58.273 --> 00:02:59.933
on, the burst happens there.

40
00:03:01.193 --> 00:03:04.693
That is why your finger clots while blood in your lung stays liquid.
